DeepClause 0.0.86: keep the original message history when no compactor ran.

Before each model call the agent passes a flattened copy of the history to the
onBeforeModelCall compaction hook and, in 0.0.86, always adopts what the hook
returns. When no compactor rewrites anything the hook returns the flattened
copy unchanged, and the tool results in it are lost, so the model no longer
sees the search_pmc results it is meant to choose papers from. This keeps the
original history unless the hook actually returned a different one.

Apply from the installed package directory:
  patch -p1 -d "$(npm root -g)/deepclause-sdk" < deepclause-0.0.86-compaction.patch

--- a/dist/agent.js
+++ b/dist/agent.js
@@ -604,7 +604,13 @@
         try {
             await tick();
             if (options.onBeforeModelCall) {
-                messages = await options.onBeforeModelCall(normalizeMessagesForCompaction(messages), lastActualInputTokens);
+                const normalizedForCompaction = normalizeMessagesForCompaction(messages);
+                const compactedMessages = await options.onBeforeModelCall(normalizedForCompaction, lastActualInputTokens);
+                // Only adopt the flattened history when a compactor actually rewrote it;
+                // otherwise keep the original messages so tool results are preserved.
+                if (compactedMessages !== normalizedForCompaction) {
+                    messages = compactedMessages;
+                }
             }
             // Ensure proper role alternation — some APIs reject consecutive same-role messages
             messages = sanitizeMessages(messages);
